From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:46:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): IME calls into libghostty need the large stack

Typing a single character into a ghostty pane through an IME took the whole
window down. Symbolized with harness/pdbaddr rather than guessed: `__chkstk`,
the stack probe, which means a stack overflow.

ghostty_surface_preedit needs more stack than the 1 MB MSVC gives Windows
Terminal's UI thread. GhosttyEngine::RunWithEngineStack exists for exactly this
and reserves 16 MB, and PLAN's ledger has said since 2026-08-04 that "any future
call into libghostty from a WT-owned thread has to be checked against this". I
added two such calls and checked neither; both now run on the big stack.

Verified by hand end to end afterwards: preedit at the cursor, candidate window,
and committed text reaching the shell.

The other half of that test is worth recording too - cascadia's IME kept working
throughout, which is the regression check on the shared TSF refactor passing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp      | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 166b4b50d..bd3575d51 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -1397,11 +1397,15 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
             return {};
         }
 
+        // Same reasoning as SetPreedit: this runs on WT's UI thread, and
+        // anything that walks into libghostty from there gets the big stack.
         double x{};
         double y{};
         double width{};
         double height{};
-        ghostty_surface_ime_point(_surface, &x, &y, &width, &height);
+        GhosttyEngine::RunWithEngineStack([&]() {
+            ghostty_surface_ime_point(_surface, &x, &y, &width, &height);
+        });
 
         // imePoint is in DIPs; _cellSize is physical.
         const auto cellWidth = _cellSize.Width / _compositionScale;
@@ -1424,8 +1428,17 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
             return;
         }
 
+        // On a large-stack thread, like every other call into libghostty that
+        // does real work. ghostty_surface_preedit needs more than the 1 MB MSVC
+        // gives WT's UI thread, and typing a single character into a ghostty
+        // pane through an IME took the whole window down with a stack overflow
+        // in __chkstk. The ledger already warned about this - "any future call
+        // into libghostty from a WT-owned thread has to be checked against
+        // this" - and this is the call that did not check.
         const auto utf8 = til::u16u8(text);
-        ghostty_surface_preedit(_surface, utf8.data(), utf8.size());
+        GhosttyEngine::RunWithEngineStack([&]() {
+            ghostty_surface_preedit(_surface, utf8.data(), utf8.size());
+        });
         _renderNow();
     }
     bool GhosttyControlCore::ForceCursorVisible() const noexcept { return false; }
